---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout>
    <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-14 pb-10">
        <h1 class="text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight leading-none md:text-7xl">
            About MLRP
        </h1>
        <!-- <p class="text-lg text-text-muted">
            The Machine Learning Reading Program (MLRP) is a student-run
            initiative at the University of Washington that connects
            undergraduates with graduate and postdoctoral researchers through
            guided reading and discussion of machine learning research papers.
        </p> -->
    </section>

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6">
        <div class="h-px bg-divider"></div>
    </div>

    <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-10">
        <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl font-semibold">Why MLRP?</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4 text-text-muted">
            <p>
                Many undergraduates interested in machine learning ask the same
                question: how do I get started in research? The usual advice
                they get is to take courses, but classroom knowledge is only
                part of what's required. The ability to read, engage, and keep
                up with current research papers, an essential skill for doing
                research, is often overlooked. MLRP aims to bridge this gap by
                connecting undergrads with machine learning researchers to build
                this skill.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6">
        <div class="h-px bg-divider"></div>
    </div>

    <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-10">
        <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl font-semibold">Contact</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4 text-text-muted">
            <p>
                If you have any suggestions, concerns, or questions about the
                program, please contact <a
                    href="mailto:jaredwd@cs.washington.edu"
                    class="text-accent underline hover:opacity-80"
                    >jaredwd@cs.washington.edu</a
                >.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

